Z||000008||thomas_l||12-22-2001||08:01 AM||||Yes, this is more of a guide for show cars. Most of what we drive fall into the 4-6 categories with a rare 3. I hate price guides  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">. Unless you have something that is extremely rare you can balance known sales prices against what you have invested and come up with a good starting point. Bottom line the price you accept from a willing buyer <I>is</I> that magic number.<P>From what I've seen Fieros (that are not show cars) tend to price out just like other 84 - 88 cars. Non runners usually &lt; $500. An average driver $500 - 1500. A nice one (usually everything works, has good paint, etc) is &gt; $1500.||||reg||1
